  <!-- Technology Difference -->
  <section id="technology" class="sdg-section sdg-section--split">
    <div class="sdg-container sdg-grid-2">
      <div>
        <h2>The Technology Difference</h2>
        <p>
          The athleisure industry has a polyester problem. Virgin polyester—petroleum-based synthetic fiber—dominates because it's inexpensive and scalable. It also generates significant environmental impact.¹
        </p>
        <p>
          ATHLOUN took a different path: We don't manufacture chemicals or invent finishes in our own lab. Instead, we curate the world's best plant-based textile technologies and apply them strategically:
        </p>
        <div class="sdg-card sdg-card--outline" style="margin-top: 20px;"><ul class="sdg-list">
          <li><b>Plant-based fabrics: </b>Cotton, bamboo, modal blends (95%+ composition)</li>
          <li><b>Plant-based finishes: </b>Best-in-class technologies from leading innovators (Chemours/Huntsman, Advantage Natural)</li>
          <li><b>Zero virgin polyester: </b>Across our entire range</li>
        </ul></div>
        <p>This isn't about having our own R&D lab. It's about intelligent curation and application—partnering with technology leaders to deliver performance without petroleum.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:grey;width: 500px;height: 550px;">
        
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Performance Technologies -->
  <section class="sdg-section sdg-section--alt">
    <div class="sdg-container fullwidth">
      <header class="sdg-section-header">
        <h2>How We Achieve Performance Without Petroleum</h2>
        <p>ATHLOUN's approach: curate best-in-class plant-based technologies and apply them intelligently to performance athleisure.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="sdg-grid-3 sdg-tech-grid">

        <article class="sdg-card">
          <h3>Teflon™ EcoElite with Zelan™ R3 Finish</h3>
          <p class="sdg-tech-tag">Renewably Sourced Stain-Repel & Wrinkle-Free Technology</p>
          <p class="sdg-tech-partner">Technology Partner: Chemours & Huntsman Textile Effects / Archroma</p>
          <p>Instead of traditional PFAS fluorocarbons or petroleum-based polymers, this finish contains 60-63% plant-based, renewably sourced materials derived from non-GMO, non-food-source feedstock.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Repels water-based stains (wine, coffee, tea, ketchup)</li>
            <li>Wrinkle-free durability (30+ washes)</li>
            <li>Maintains fabric breathability</li>
            <li>USDA Biobased certified, GOTS-approved, Bluesign® approved</li>
          </ul>
          {% comment %} <p class="sdg-tech-products">Why it matters: First renewably sourced water-repellent finish in the industry. Three times more durable than existing non-fluorinated alternatives.</p> {% endcomment %}
          <p class="sdg-tech-products">Products: Travel Polo, Luxe Vee</p>
        </article>

        <article class="sdg-card">
          <h3>EcoEMO™ with Enliven Technology</h3>
          <p class="sdg-tech-tag">Patented Neem & Tulsi Botanical Infusion (IN 318405)</p>
          <p class="sdg-tech-partner">Technology Partner: Advantage Natural (India)</p>
          <p>Instead of synthetic antimicrobials (silver nanoparticles, triclosan), this patented technology infuses fabrics with concentrated extracts of neem (Azadirachta Indica) and tulsi (Ocimum Sanctum)—plants used in Ayurvedic medicine for centuries.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Anti-microbial: 100% bacterial reduction (AATCC100 standards, 30+ washes)</li>
<li>Anti-odor: Natural bacterial growth prevention</li>
<li>UPF 20+ sun protection (AATCC183 standards)</li>
<li>Insect-repellent properties</li>
<li>Skin-friendly: Reduces irritation</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="sdg-tech-products">Products: EcoEMO Polo, EcoEMO Crew</p>
        </article>

        <article class="sdg-card">
          <h3>AquaSave Melange Technology</h3>
          <p class="sdg-tech-tag">90% Water Consumption Reduction</p>
          <p class="sdg-tech-partner">ATHLOUN's Innovation: Strategic yarn construction using melange (blended) fibres.</p>
          <p>Our process consumes 1.4 litres of water per garment versus industry standard of 14-15 litres—a 90% reduction through intelligent fibre blending (cotton, bamboo, modal) and responsible sourcing.</p>
          {% comment %} <ul>
            <li></li>
          </ul> {% endcomment %}
          <p class="sdg-tech-products">Products: AquaSave Melange Crew</p>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

